<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><title>Privacy — Cadastre</title><meta name="description" content="Privacy information for Cadastre's public reference catalog and images."/></head><body><header class="site-header shell legal-header"><a href="/" class="wordmark">cadastre<span class="wordmark-dot">.</span></a><a href="/catalog" class="header-access">Browse the catalog ↗</a></header><main class="shell legal-page"><p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY NOTICE</p><h1>Public research.<br/>Simple access.</h1><p class="legal-version">Effective 26 October 2026</p><p>Cadastre is a Kenshiki Labs research initiative. Its source catalog and published reference images are available without an account, application, organization verification, or access key.</p><h2>Browsing the collection</h2><p>The site retrieves the public source index, image metadata, and reference images from Cadastre. It uses self-hosted fonts and assets. Service infrastructure may process request metadata, including network addresses and access logs, for operation and security. Do not submit personal identity documents or license numbers to this reference website.</p><h2>Source provenance</h2><p>Public records identify source publications, source fingerprints, and research status. Specimen images are research references from collected publications; they are not records submitted by people seeking identity verification.</p><h2>Operator records</h2><p>Administrative operations remain authenticated. Any records retained from earlier research-access applications are separate from the public catalog and are not published. Those records may include organization and applicant information, domain proof, attestations, and review history. This service does not promise an automated deletion schedule.</p><h2>Questions and requests</h2><p>For privacy questions, corrections, or deletion requests about earlier applications, contact the maintainers through the <a href="https://github.com/Kenshiki-Labs/state-id-harvester/issues">Cadastre repository</a>. Do not post personal application details, claim tokens, or operator keys in public issues. A maintainer can arrange an appropriate channel.</p><p><a href="/">← Return to Cadastre</a> · <a href="/acceptable-use">Acceptable use</a></p></main></body></html>
